<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor5e75fe5b-5b13-4a83-8b8b-f5bd68563b14" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <h2 class="subhead1" data-pasted="true" style="text-align: center;"><strong>STATE ELECTION</strong></h2><h2 class="subhead1" style="text-align: center;"><strong>TUESDAY, NOVEMBER 3, 2026</strong></h2><h2 class="subhead1" style="text-align: center;"><strong>&nbsp;Polls open from 7:00 am to 8:00 pm at Town Hall</strong></h2><h3 style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-family: Raleway; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(30, 52, 76); font-size: 1.3em; text-decoration: none; display: block; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);" data-pasted="true">Sample Ballots</h3><ul><li>Click <a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1216" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>here</strong></a> to view the ballot</li></ul><h3 style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-family: Raleway; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(30, 52, 76); font-size: 1.3em; text-decoration: none; display: block; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);" data-pasted="true">In-Person Early Voting</h3><p><strong>Begins on Saturday, October 17th - October 30th at the Town Hall. &nbsp;</strong><strong>Click</strong><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1215" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>here</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong></a><strong>for the dates and hours and further information on In-Person Early Voting for the State Election.</strong></p><h3 style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-family: Raleway; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(30, 52, 76); font-size: 1.3em; text-decoration: none; display: block; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);" data-pasted="true">Voter Registration</h3><p>Deadline to register to vote for the State Election is Saturday, October 24, 2026. &nbsp;Click <a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/OVR/">here</a> for to register to vote online or <a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/divisions/elections/download/voter-registration-forms/voter-registration_English.pdf">here</a> to download a voter registration form. &nbsp;You can also register to vote in-person at the Town Clerk&apos;s Office during regular business hours and the Town Clerk&apos;s Office will be open on Saturday,October 24, 2026 from 9:00 am to 5:00 pm for voter registration.</p><h3 style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-family: Raleway; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(30, 52, 76); font-size: 1.3em; text-decoration: none; display: block; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);" data-pasted="true">Vote by Mail</h3><p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1.4em; color: rgb(54, 54, 54); font-family: Raleway; font-size: 15.2px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;">All registered voters qualify to vote by mail. Voter&apos;s can apply online on the State&apos;s portal <a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/MailInRequestWeb/MailInBallot.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Mail in Ballot Application Opens in new window" style="box-sizing: border-box; overflow-wrap: anywhere; word-break: normal; color: rgb(112, 51, 37); text-decoration: underline;">Online Mail in Ballot Application</a>&nbsp; or download an application <a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/divisions/elections/download/vote-by-mail-applications/Vote-by-Mail-Paper-Application-2025.pdf">here</a> for a mail in ballot. <strong style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;">Any mail-in ballot must be requested in writing by 5 p.m. on the Tuesday, October 27, 2026. Your application can only be accepted if it has reached your local election office by the deadline. Apply as early as possible, especially if your ballot will need to be mailed out of town. The U.S. Postal Service recommends allowing up to 7 days for mail delivery. To ensure you receive your ballot with enough time to mail it back, you should apply 2-3 weeks before Election Day.</strong>&nbsp;</p><h3 style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-family: Raleway; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(30, 52, 76); font-size: 1.3em; text-decoration: none; display: block; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);">Request a Mail Ballot</h3><p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1.4em; color: rgb(54, 54, 54); font-family: Raleway; font-size: 15.2px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;">To request a vote by mail ballot you need to send a letter requesting the ballot be mailed to your home. Be sure to include your name, address, state the election you want it for, and sign the letter. Every person requesting a ballot must sign a request. The ballot will be mailed to you.&nbsp;</p><h3 style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-family: Raleway; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(30, 52, 76); font-size: 1.3em; text-decoration: none; display: block; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);">How to Submit Your Vote by Mail Application</h3><ul style="box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px 0px 1.4em; padding: 0px 0px 0px 3em; font-family: Raleway; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; color: rgb(54, 54, 54); line-height: 1.5; list-style-type: circle; font-size: 15.2px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"><li style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0.35em;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;">By mail</strong> - Mail signed application to the Town Clerk&apos;s Office, 584 Main Street, Suite 10, Athol MA 01331</li><li style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0.35em;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;">Drop Box</strong> - Drop signed application in Drop Box located in front of the Town Hall - Accessible Drop Box located on side of Town Hall</li><li style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0.35em;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;">Email</strong> the signed application to <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="56203922331622392138393037223e393a78392431">[email&#160;protected]</a></li><li style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0.35em;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;">Fax</strong> the signed application to 978-249-2491</li><li style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0.35em;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;">In Person</strong> - Office hours are Monday, Wednesday, and Thursday 8:00 am to 5:00 pm; Tuesday 8:00 am to 8:00 pm; Closed Friday</li></ul><h3 style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-family: Raleway; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(30, 52, 76); font-size: 1.3em; text-decoration: none; display: block; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);">Return of Vote by Mail Ballots</h3><p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1.4em; color: rgb(54, 54, 54); font-family: Raleway; font-size: 15.2px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;">All ballots for an Election <strong style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;">must&nbsp;</strong>be received by the close of polls on the day of the Election. Mail-In Ballots include a return ballot envelope that is addressed to the Town Clerk&apos;s Office. Ballots <strong style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;">cannot&nbsp;</strong>be returned to the polling location on Election Day. They can be put in the drop box no later than the close of polls on Election Day.</p><p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1.4em; color: rgb(54, 54, 54); font-family: Raleway; font-size: 15.2px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;">Voters who receive a mail-in ballot but do not return it prior to Election Day may appear to vote in person to cast a ballot on Election Day. Any voter that has returned a vote by mail ballot is not permitted to appear to vote in person on Election Day.</p><h3 style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-family: Raleway; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(30, 52, 76); font-size: 1.3em; text-decoration: none; display: block; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);" data-pasted="true">Campaigning on Election Day or Early Voting:</h3><p>No poster, card, handbill, placard, picture or circular intended to influence the action of the voter, other than those expressly authorized by M.G.L. c.54 &sect;65, shall be posted, exhibited, circulated or distributed in the building where the polling location is located, on the walls thereof, on the premises located at 584 Main Street, stand within one hundred and fifty feet (150&apos;) of the building entrance door to said Polling Location on Election Day or during Early Voting.</p><p>For further information, please call the Town Clerk&apos;s Office at 978-721-8445 or email at <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#1d6b7269785d69726a73727b7c6975727133726f7a">Email Town of Athol</a>.</p>
    </div>

